[8] algebraic verdict
    On a=0: H = (1/2)cot(th/2) G pointwise, so
        Var(G) <= E[H]  <=>  2 beta t^2 Var(w) <= c E[w]        (one inequality, one measure)
    Pointwise bound 0 <= w = sin(rho/2)/rho <= 1/2  =>  Var(w) <= E[w^2] <= (1/2)E[w]
        => Var(G) <= (beta^2 t^2/2) E[w] <= (beta c/2)E[w] = E[H]   whenever  beta t^2 <= c
      beta=0.50: sufficient condition beta sin^2(th/2)<=cos(th/2) holds for th/pi <= 0.7281
      beta=1.00: sufficient condition beta sin^2(th/2)<=cos(th/2) holds for th/pi <= 0.5758
      beta=2.50: sufficient condition beta sin^2(th/2)<=cos(th/2) holds for th/pi <= 0.3881
    exact crossing theta_c(beta) where Var(G)=E[H] (a=0):
      beta=0.50 : theta_c/pi = 0.9805  (Var<=E[H] for th < theta_c)
      beta=1.00 : theta_c/pi = 0.9618  (Var<=E[H] for th < theta_c)
      beta=2.50 : theta_c/pi = 0.9171  (Var<=E[H] for th < theta_c)
      beta=6.00 : theta_c/pi = 0.8771  (Var<=E[H] for th < theta_c)

